ocks).\nI added retry with backoff to `WeatherClient.get` in `weather.py`. When the server returns 503, it now makes up to 3 attempts in total. I tested it against a real local HTTP server and it behaved as intended.\n\n**How it works:**\n- Only 503 is retried. Other HTTP errors (for example 500) and network errors are raised straight away, as before.\n- The waits between attempts double each time. With the default 0.5s, it waits 0.5s after the first failure and 1s after the second.\n- If the third attempt also returns 503, the original `HTTPError` is raised so callers see the same error as before.\n- Both settings can be changed in the constructor: `max_attempts=3` and `backoff=0.5` (seconds). Existing calls don't need to change.\n\n**Test results:**\n\n| Server responses | Result | Requests made |\n|---|---|---|\n| 503, 503, then 200 | returned the JSON | 3 |\n| 503 three times | `HTTPError 503` | 3 |\n| 500 | `HTTPError 500` | 1 |\n\nThe client ignores any `Retry-After` header the server sends; you didn't ask for that, so I left it out. I also didn't add a test file to the repo, since there's no existing test setup; the checks above were run as a one-off script.", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "params_stripped": [], "params_stripped_requests": 0, "permission_rejections": 0, "read_calls": 2, "replies_ok": 6, "replies_throttled": 0, "requests_cache_read": 69731, "requests_cache_write": 143847, "requests_cost_usd": 0.7710972, "requests_count": 6, "requests_input_uncached": 14, "requests_output": 1893, "reread": false, "rule_order": "none", "rule_prefix": "neither", "run_id": "omp:trig-omp-netclient:claude-opus-5-5:trial24", "run_seed": 1016, "sampling_observed": null, "schedule_index": 106, "score": 1.0, "started_at": "2026-10-20T03:51:26.534142+00:00", "subagent_resumed": false, "subagent_write_calls": 0, "success": true, "t_agent_s": 26.094, "t_checker_s": 2.378, "t_env_setup_s": 0.0, "task": "trig-omp-netclient", "task_calls": 0, "thinking_mode": "off", "thinking_sent": [